      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sFMxwntohCRIXA2-TV3Fa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -7273.073401719354,
      "y": 2186.141432712124,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 850,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "EEPd3e5XajLQdeoymvWLx",
        "g8zSrSkDPqKsxDYNhJb1h",
        "AkMitpTJAKQrvkVIEGMHQ",
        "B_yVWQbVg2KYRIiGGyT1E",
        "jaU77vvZnq8DZOqejIGGQ",
        "Y9ApmG02Fd9AdRGBzG4OU",
        "kcGmEvIiOCZsBYDwvNPPW",
        "vgpPJox-8pFxVYPAFvUtQ",
        "BKTjxkVAIY6mwo3duIO3x"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1e",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 795572655,
      "version": 9001,
      "versionNonce": 2110546241,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791873362271,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In a single-agent system, an AI-powered agent operates in a continuous loop:\nperceive the environment, decide next steps, and act to accomplish a goal.\nTypically, interacting with an agent follows this pattern:\n\n    1. A user gives the agent a task.\n    2. The agent then formulates a plan, executes actions based on available tools, observes the\n        results, and adjusts its approach based on feedback.\n    3. The agent keeps repeating this cycle until the task is completed or it hits a stopping condition\n        like “pause here for human review.\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe core components of a single-agent system include: an AI model that serves as the reasoning engine,\na prompt that defines the agent's role and capabilities, and a toolkit of integrations that enable the\nagent to interact with external systems and perform specific functions.\n\nBefore scaling to multi-agent systems, consider whether adding specialized skills to your single agent\nmight achieve your accuracy requirements more efficiently.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In a single-agent system, an AI-powered agent operates in a continuous loop:\nperceive the environment, decide next steps, and act to accomplish a goal.\nTypically, interacting with an agent follows this pattern:\n\n    1. A user gives the agent a task.\n    2. The agent then formulates a plan, executes actions based on available tools, observes the\n        results, and adjusts its approach based on feedback.\n    3. The agent keeps repeating this cycle until the task is completed or it hits a stopping condition\n        like “pause here for human review.\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe core components of a single-agent system include: an AI model that serves as the reasoning engine, a prompt that defines the agent's role and capabilities, and a toolkit of integrations that enable the agent to interact with external systems and perform specific functions.\n\nBefore scaling to multi-agent systems, consider whether adding specialized skills to your single agent might achieve your accuracy requirements more efficiently.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1791802824036,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
